      "id": "1p47o40",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of the Maratha Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj laid the foundation of the Maratha Kingdom, establishing Raigad as his capital.",
        "The Maratha administration was run by the 'Ashta Pradhan' (council of eight ministers), with the Peshwa as the Prime Minister.",
        "The Maratha military excelled in 'Ganimi Kava' (guerilla warfare), leveraging the rugged terrain of the Western Ghats.",
        "The revenue system was based on Malik Ambar's system and included major levies like Chauth (1/4th land revenue) and Sardeshmukhi (an extra 10%).",
        "Post-Shivaji, the empire was consolidated and vastly expanded under the line of hereditary Peshwas."
      ],
      "id": "dw0ox4r"
    },
